//! Conformance harness entry. Wires the helpers (`_helpers.rs`) and the
//! per-case tests (`_generated.rs`, `_generated_v4.rs`) into a single cargo
//! integration-test binary: fixed predicates and EvalContexts whose verdicts the
//! contract must keep.
//!
//! Run with:
//!   cargo test --test conformance -p policy-interpreter
//!
//! The cases were generated by the TypeScript synthesiser and reference
//! evaluator of the grammar-4 and grammar-6 packages. Both are gone (the
//! TypeScript side has no evaluator any more: simulate and verify call the
//! contract's own `check`), so the files are kept as they are and are not
//! regenerated. The cross-layer gate for the grammar-7 wire format is
//! `tests/parity.rs`, which writes the corpus the TypeScript codec is tested
//! against (`packages/policy-synth/fixtures/parity/grammar7.json`).
//!
//! `_generated.rs` covers the predicate a recording synthesises. `_generated_v4.rs`
//! covers the grammar-4 operators, which the recording path cannot reach: its
//! deny-case mutators cannot violate a scaled bound, and they skip `or` because
//! violating one branch proves nothing while another can still permit.

mod _generated;
mod _generated_v4;
mod _helpers;
